C03: a long declarative statement is not an unanswered knowledge question, so the overheard-speech clarification stands in English (KNOW1835)

KNOW1833 measured: «Water expands when it freezes, that is why pipes burst in winter, at least that is what they told me.» carried «why» and «what», the App's knowledge_not_answered rule rejected the mind's overheard-speech clarification because it asks, and the fallback echoed the statement. The rule now steps aside for a long statement with no question mark whose ask words never lead a clause.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


